; Otter Raid -- text / HUD charset (hires 8x8, one colour per cell)
;
;   .  background      #  foreground (cell colour chosen by the engine)
;
; RULE: row 7 (the 8th row) of EVERY glyph must stay empty -- a raster
; split happens on that line.  tools/gfx.py rejects any glyph that
; breaks it.  $80-$FF stay empty (reserved for a title logo).
;
; @tchars at=$xx [names=...] [color=n]: glyphs are laid out side by
; side, 8 rows per band; codes run left to right, band after band.
; color= is only the preview colour.

; ===================================================================
; Font $00-$3F, C64 screen-code order.  Arcade style, 7x7, 2px stems.
; ===================================================================
@tchars at=$00
.#####.. ..###... ######.. ..####.. #####... #######. #######. ..#####.
